{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the S3 repair at head a41b640ad8fd1ac18b7ac642cb881e14881f8e3e, tree ef7e6940, for request 7951d998 and review request 6d3581b5. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds two commits to the reviewed head bfca55ea. I read the note first, then the diff, against item 1 of review 9a44d98b and correction 85e018c2. That review's findings on the successor definition, the preserved pins, the authority rules and the six witnesses stand.\n\n## Item 1 of 9a44d98b\n\nResolved. `withdraw-approval-request` loses exactly the two guards named: the ask's state and equality with the ask's current body. It keeps `state: open`, the requester signer and equality with the request's own `bodyAt`, so the act stays bound to its text. `approve` and `decide` keep their current-text guards, and withdrawal supplies no verdict. A final state frees live capacity without raising `max: 64`.\n\nThe same native journey now shows that:\n\n- the requester withdraws a stale request with its original body after a revision;\n- a nonrequester holding `issue.comment` is refused;\n- the requester supplying the newer body is refused `stale-question`;\n- the requester withdraws a surviving request after the ask is decided, and both requests read back as `withdrawn` with their original references.\n\nThe new control restores only the old ask-current-body equality and repins only the successor. The positive stale withdrawal then fails on an ordinary `AssertionError`, and all three files are restored exactly.\n\nThe note records the correction, withdrawing the bound-edge claim and the unverified comparison with the old lane.\n\n## The gates\n\nThe gate at 50cafdae, tree f6a113d7, passes all five stages. Its receipt exits 0 with complete capture, the same source before and after, and no dropped bytes. Node passes 80 cases, Counting 56, Plain 3,146 with one skip and Native 860 with two skips. From 50cafdae to the head, only the note and the manifest change.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5068dab4 gives the head tree ef7e6940.\n- The new pin is `sha256:88e763ab`. The canonical file, digest module, export and generated reference agree, and no historical byte changes.\n- I ran the owning files once each: `issue-questions.test.ts` and `definitions.test.ts`, 5 of 5; the native `issue-questions.scope.test.ts`, 1 of 1. The builder worktree stayed clean.\n- The evidence verifies. The manifest has SHA-256 da3293bc and 36,882 bytes. All 217 cited files match across both roots. The original directory still has 237 files and 77,322,503 bytes. The repair directory has 419 files and 148,259,732 bytes, its external manifest c9c785c0 matches all 419 rows, and in both directories `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with no file unlisted or writable.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 761 links, 0 broken. check-notes from 5068dab4: 0 warnings. check-commit-messages: 4 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. `approval` still has `max: 256`, and its only state isn't final, so verdicts in one issue stop at 256 for good. This fails closed.\n2. A block on a withdrawn ask has no release through `decide`. I haven't compared this with the old lane, and the block's owner may need another way out when S4 or a later slice reads blocks.\n3. S4's `needs_you` should still treat a request on older text as stale, not as work, because withdrawal closes it only if the requester acts.\n\n## Architecture\n\nAn opt-in successor under existing forms, with older rooms untouched. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nAuthority is unchanged, and a member can no longer exhaust the type for good, since the requester can close each request. A request's own requester can still leave requests open up to the limit, within one issue they can already write to. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe repair removes two guards and adds no act. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the repair holds, with its control, and the original conditions stand. Disposition of 9a44d98b: resolved.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing. No Worker serves this definition, so no deploy is due. If S1 has landed when this one is ready, the request asks for the activation to join `examples/repo-in-ai/runbook.md`; S1 hasn't landed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e85d756960e153befeb687a914500878b036c2b0","binding":"assigned","head":"a41b640ad8fd1ac18b7ac642cb881e14881f8e3e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:beaac3ec35cdda92353587e0233997dbeb534225\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2800149a8a445ab650cc1c7b8f18820ec603a7a0\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:beaac3ec35cdda92353587e0233997dbeb534225","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}